      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Keep It Running: An AI Trustworthiness Simulation</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"app-shell\">\n  <header class=\"app-header\">\n    <h1 class=\"app-title\">Keep It Running</h1>\n    <div id=\"trust-badge\" class=\"trust-badge\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\" hidden>\n      <span class=\"trust-badge-label\">Trust Score</span>\n      <span id=\"trust-badge-value\" class=\"trust-badge-value\">70</span>\n      <span class=\"trust-badge-max\">out of 100</span>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n  <main id=\"app-main\" class=\"app-main\">\n    <noscript>\n      <p class=\"noscript-message\">This activity needs JavaScript turned on in your browser to run.</p>\n    </noscript>\n  </main>\n</div>\n<script src=\"script.js\" defer></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "contents": "/* ---------- Design tokens ---------- */\n:root {\n  --color-bg: #f7f3ff;\n  --color-surface: #ffffff;\n  --color-text: #241b3a;\n  --color-text-muted: #524a67;\n\n  --color-primary: #6d28d9;\n  --color-primary-dark: #5b21b6;\n  --color-secondary: #be123c;\n  --color-secondary-dark: #9f1239;\n  --color-accent: #fcd34d;\n  --color-teal: #0f766e;\n  --color-teal-dark: #115e59;\n  --color-success: #047857;\n  --color-danger: #b91c1c;\n  --color-focus: #1d4ed8;\n\n  --radius-md: 12px;\n  --radius-lg: 20px;\n  --space-1: 0.5rem;\n  --space-2: 0.75rem;\n  --space-3: 1rem;\n  --space-4: 1.5rem;\n  --space-5: 2rem;\n\n  --shadow-card: 0 6px 20px rgba(36, 27, 58, 0.12);\n}\n\n/* ---------- Reset ---------- */\n*, *::before, *::after {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-family: -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\n  color: var(--color-text);\n  background-color: var(--color-bg);\n  line-height: 1.55;\n}\n\nh1, h2, h3, h4 {\n  margin: 0 0 var(--space-2) 0;\n  line-height: 1.2;\n}\n\np {\n  margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) 0;\n}\n\nfieldset {\n  border: none;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  font: inherit;\n}\n\n/* ---------- Focus visibility (used everywhere) ---------- */\nbutton:focus-visible,\na:focus-visible,\ninput:focus-visible,\ntextarea:focus-visible,\nsummary:focus-visible {\n  outline: none;\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #ffffff, 0 0 0 5px var(--color-focus);\n}\n\n.system-radio:focus-visible,\n.action-radio:focus-visible {\n  box-shadow: none;\n}\n\n.system-radio:focus-visible + .system-card-body,\n.action-radio:focus-visible + .action-card-body {\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #ffffff, 0 0 0 5px var(--color-focus);\n}\n\n/* ---------- Layout shell ---------- */\n.app-shell {\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n}\n\n.app-header {\n  background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-primary), var(--color-secondary));\n  color: #ffffff;\n  padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  gap: var(--space-2);\n}\n\n.app-title {\n  font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.trust-badge {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: baseline;\n  gap: var(--space-1);\n  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);\n  border: 2px solid #ffffff;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);\n  font-weight: 700;\n}\n\n.trust-badge-label {\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.trust-badge-value {\n  font-size: 1.25rem;\n}\n\n.trust-badge-max {\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.app-main {\n  flex: 1;\n  width: min(920px, 100%);\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-4) var(--space-5);\n}\n\n.noscript-message {\n  background-color: var(--color-accent);\n  padding: var(--space-3);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  font-weight: 700;\n}\n\n/* ---------- Screen text ---------- */\n.screen-eyebrow {\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.06em;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: var(--color-secondary-dark);\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n}\n\n.screen-heading {\n  font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.1rem);\n  color: var(--color-primary-dark);\n}\n\n.screen-lead {\n  font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.2vw, 1.15rem);\n  color: var(--color-text);\n}\n\n.screen-body {\n  color: var(--color-text-muted);\n}\n\n.subheading {\n  font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.35rem);\n  color: var(--color-primary-dark);\n  margin-top: var(--space-4);\n}\n\n/* ---------- Cards ---------- */\n.card {\n  background-color: var(--color-surface);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);\n  padding: var(--space-4);\n}\n\n.card-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));\n  gap: var(--space-3);\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-4);\n}\n\n/* ---------- System selection cards ---------- */\n.system-card {\n  position: relative;\n  display: block;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.system-radio {\n  position: absolute;\n  width: 1px;\n  height: 1px;\n  margin: -1px;\n  opacity: 0;\n}\n\n.system-card-body {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: var(--space-1);\n  background-color: var(--color-surface);\n  border: 3px solid transparent;\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);\n  padding: var(--space-4);\n  height: 100%;\n}\n\n.system-radio:checked + .system-card-body {\n  border-color: var(--color-primary);\n  background-color: #f2e9ff;\n}\n\n.system-card:hover .system-card-body {\n  border-color: var(--color-primary);\n}\n\n.system-name {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  font-size: 1.1rem;\n  color: var(--color-primary-dark);\n}\n\n.system-desc {\n  color: var(--color-text-muted);\n}\n\n/* ---------- Spec card (definition list) ---------- */\n.spec-card {\n  background-color: var(--color-surface);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);\n  padding: var(--space-4);\n  margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;\n}\n\n.spec-card-term {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: var(--color-teal-dark);\n  margin-top: var(--space-2);\n}\n\n.spec-card-term:first-child {\n  margin-top: 0;\n}\n\n.spec-card-value {\n  margin: 0.2rem 0 0 0;\n  color: var(--color-text);\n}\n\n/* ---------- Two column layout ---------- */\n.two-col {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: var(--space-4);\n  align-items: flex-start;\n}\n\n.two-col-side {\n  flex: 1 1 260px;\n}\n\n.two-col-main {\n  flex: 2 1 320px;\n}\n\n/* ---------- Forms and fields ---------- */\n.field-stack {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: var(--space-3);\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-3);\n}\n\n.field-group {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 0.35rem;\n}\n\n.field-label {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: var(--color-primary-dark);\n}\n\n.field-hint {\n  color: var(--color-text-muted);\n  font-size: 0.95rem;\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n.field-textarea {\n  font: inherit;\n  color: var(--color-text);\n  border: 2px solid #d9cdf5;\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  padding: var(--space-2);\n  resize: vertical;\n  min-height: 3.5rem;\n  width: 100%;\n}\n\n.field-textarea:focus {\n  border-color: var(--color-primary);\n}\n\n/* ---------- Action selection cards ---------- */\n.action-fieldset {\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-3);\n}\n\n.action-legend {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  font-size: 1.1rem;\n  color: var(--color-primary-dark);\n  padding: 0;\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-2);\n}\n\n.action-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));\n  gap: var(--space-3);\n}\n\n.action-card {\n  position: relative;\n  display: block;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.action-radio {\n  position: absolute;\n  width: 1px;\n  height: 1px;\n  margin: -1px;\n  opacity: 0;\n}\n\n.action-card-body {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 0.3rem;\n  background-color: var(--color-surface);\n  border: 3px solid #e4d9fb;\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  padding: var(--space-3);\n  height: 100%;\n}\n\n.action-radio:checked + .action-card-body {\n  border-color: var(--color-teal);\n  background-color: #e6f4f2;\n}\n\n.action-card:hover .action-card-body {\n  border-color: var(--color-teal);\n}\n\n.action-card-disabled {\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n\n.action-card-disabled .action-card-body {\n  background-color: #f0edf7;\n  color: var(--color-text-muted);\n}\n\n.action-name {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: var(--color-primary-dark);\n}\n\n.action-hint {\n  color: var(--color-text-muted);\n  font-size: 0.95rem;\n}\n\n.action-remaining {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  color: var(--color-secondary-dark);\n}\n\n/* ---------- Buttons ---------- */\n.btn {\n  display: inline-block;\n  border: none;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  min-height: 44px;\n  padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;\n  transition: transform 0.12s ease, background-color 0.12s ease;\n}\n\n.btn:hover {\n  transform: translateY(-2px);\n}\n\n.btn-large {\n  font-size: 1.05rem;\n}\n\n.btn-primary {\n  background-color: var(--color-primary);\n  color: #ffffff;\n}\n\n.btn-primary:hover {\n  background-color: var(--color-primary-dark);\n}\n\n.btn-secondary {\n  background-color: #ffffff;\n  color: var(--color-primary-dark);\n  border: 2px solid var(--color-primary);\n}\n\n.btn-secondary:hover {\n  background-color: #f2e9ff;\n}\n\n.button-row {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: var(--space-2);\n}\n\n/* ---------- Event card ---------- */\n.event-card {\n  border-inline-start: 8px solid var(--color-accent);\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-4);\n}\n\n.event-text {\n  font-size: 1.1rem;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.event-signal {\n  color: var(--color-text-muted);\n  margin-bottom: 0;\n}\n\n/* ---------- Results screen ---------- */\n.results-outcome {\n  border-inline-start: 8px solid var(--color-teal);\n}\n\n.results-score-line {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  font-size: 1.1rem;\n}\n\n.counterfactual-list {\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-4);\n}\n\n.counterfactual-details {\n  background-color: var(--color-surface);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);\n  padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-2);\n}\n\n.counterfactual-summary {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: var(--color-primary-dark);\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.counterfactual-text {\n  margin: var(--space-2) 0 0 0;\n  color: var(--color-text);\n}\n\n/* ---------- Maintain screen ---------- */\n.stale-flag {\n  display: inline-block;\n  background-color: var(--color-danger);\n  color: #ffffff;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 0.2rem 0.75rem;\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n}\n\n/* ---------- Decision log table ---------- */\n.table-scroll {\n  overflow-x: auto;\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-4);\n}\n\n.log-table {\n  border-collapse: collapse;\n  width: 100%;\n  min-width: 640px;\n  background-color: var(--color-surface);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n.log-table caption {\n  text-align: start;\n  color: var(--color-text-muted);\n  padding: var(--space-2);\n  font-style: italic;\n}\n\n.log-table th,\n.log-table td {\n  text-align: start;\n  padding: var(--space-2);\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #e4d9fb;\n  vertical-align: top;\n}\n\n.log-table thead th {\n  background-color: var(--color-primary);\n  color: #ffffff;\n}\n\n/* ---------- Statement review ---------- */\n.statement-field {\n  background-color: var(--color-surface);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);\n  padding: var(--space-3);\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-3);\n}\n\n.statement-field-label {\n  color: var(--color-teal-dark);\n  margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n}\n\n.version-history-list {\n  margin: var(--space-2) 0 0 0;\n  padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;\n}\n\n.turn-in-block {\n  background-color: var(--color-surface);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);\n  padding: var(--space-4);\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: var(--space-2);\n  margin-bottom: var(--space-4);\n}\n\n.summary-textarea {\n  font-family: ui-monospace, \"SFMono-Regular\", Consolas, monospace;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  background-color: var(--color-bg);\n  min-height: 12rem;\n}\n\n.fatal-error {\n  background-color: var(--color-danger);\n  color: #ffffff;\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  padding: var(--space-3);\n  font-weight: 700;\n}\n\n/* ---------- Responsive ---------- */\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n  .app-header {\n    flex-direction: column;\n    align-items: flex-start;\n  }\n\n  .btn-large {\n    width: 100%;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n\n  .button-row {\n    flex-direction: column;\n  }\n}\n\n/* ---------- Reduced motion ---------- */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  * {\n    transition-duration: 0.001ms !important;\n    animation-duration: 0.001ms !important;\n  }\n\n  .btn:hover {\n    transform: none;\n  }\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "script.js",
          "contents": "// ---------- Content data ----------\n\nconst SYSTEMS = {\n  playlist: {\n    name: \"Playlist Recommender\",\n    tagline: \"Suggests songs based on listening history.\",\n    purpose: \"Suggests songs to listeners based on their past listening history.\",\n    trainingData: \"Two years of listening logs from current users.\",\n    accuracyClaim: \"91% of suggested songs get played all the way through.\",\n    events: {\n      drift: {\n        text: \"A new music genre has exploded in popularity, and it is flooding recommendations with artists the model rates poorly.\",\n        signal: \"Accuracy on the last 500 plays has slipped from 91% to 78%, and it is still falling.\"\n      },\n      databug: {\n        text: \"Play counts for a small set of songs have jumped to ten times their normal rate overnight.\",\n        signal: \"There is no matching increase in actual listening sessions for those songs.\"\n      },\n      usageshift: {\n        text: \"The app just launched in three new countries.\",\n        signal: \"Listening data from the new regions barely resembles the training data.\"\n      },\n      falsealarm: {\n        text: \"A joke playlist went viral overnight.\",\n        signal: \"Odd recommendations spiked for about six hours, and the spike is already fading.\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  studybuddy: {\n    name: \"Study Buddy\",\n    tagline: \"A homework-help chatbot that answers subject questions.\",\n    purpose: \"Answers student questions about homework across core subjects.\",\n    trainingData: \"Textbook question-and-answer pairs and past tutoring transcripts for grades 9 through 12.\",\n    accuracyClaim: \"88% of answers are rated helpful by student testers.\",\n    events: {\n      drift: {\n        text: \"Students have started writing in a new slang-heavy style the model was not trained to parse.\",\n        signal: \"Helpful ratings have dropped from 88% to 74% over the past two weeks.\"\n      },\n      databug: {\n        text: \"A batch of submissions is being logged twice and double-flagged for plagiarism.\",\n        signal: \"The flag rate for one class period has tripled with no change in the essays themselves.\"\n      },\n      usageshift: {\n        text: \"The school just rolled the tool out to sixth graders for the first time.\",\n        signal: \"The tool was built and tested only on grades 9 through 12 material.\"\n      },\n      falsealarm: {\n        text: \"One class was assigned an identical essay prompt.\",\n        signal: \"The plagiarism-flag rate spiked for 30 structurally similar but original essays, and it is already settling.\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  delivery: {\n    name: \"Delivery ETA Predictor\",\n    tagline: \"Estimates delivery time for a food and rideshare app.\",\n    purpose: \"Estimates how long a delivery will take for a food and rideshare app.\",\n    trainingData: \"One year of trip data from three established cities.\",\n    accuracyClaim: \"Estimates land within five minutes, 90% of the time.\",\n    events: {\n      drift: {\n        text: \"A new expressway opened, and traffic patterns nearby have shifted.\",\n        signal: \"On-time estimates near the new route have slipped from 90% to 76%.\"\n      },\n      databug: {\n        text: \"A sync error is logging some driver timestamps twice.\",\n        signal: \"Delivery windows for a subset of drivers are logging as physically impossible.\"\n      },\n      usageshift: {\n        text: \"The app just expanded into a rural service area.\",\n        signal: \"The new area has a fraction of the address density the model trained on.\"\n      },\n      falsealarm: {\n        text: \"A stadium concert let out all at once.\",\n        signal: \"ETAs near the venue spiked for two hours and are already trending back to normal.\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  caption: {\n    name: \"Caption Generator\",\n    tagline: \"Auto-writes captions and alt text for photos on a social app.\",\n    purpose: \"Writes captions and alt text for photos posted on a social app.\",\n    trainingData: \"500,000 tagged photos from the app's most active users.\",\n    accuracyClaim: \"85% of captions are rated accurate by human reviewers.\",\n    events: {\n      drift: {\n        text: \"A new photo style is sweeping the app, and captions keep missing the point of it.\",\n        signal: \"Accuracy ratings on the new-style photos have dropped from 85% to 69%.\"\n      },\n      databug: {\n        text: \"A metadata bug is attaching the same three tags to every photo uploaded from one type of device.\",\n        signal: \"Tag diversity for that device type has dropped to near zero, while other devices are unaffected.\"\n      },\n      usageshift: {\n        text: \"The app just added support for users who are blind or low-vision.\",\n        signal: \"This group relies on captions far more heavily than the training population did.\"\n      },\n      falsealarm: {\n        text: \"A viral meme photo format spread through the app for a day.\",\n        signal: \"Captions look repetitive because thousands of near-identical images arrived at once, and the wave is already passing.\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst SYSTEM_ORDER = [\"playlist\", \"studybuddy\", \"delivery\", \"caption\"];\n\nconst ACTIONS = {\n  monitor: {\n    label: \"Monitor & Wait\",\n    hint: \"Keep watching. Make no changes yet.\"\n  },\n  retrain: {\n    label: \"Retrain or Adjust the Model\",\n    hint: \"Update the model with new data. Limited uses this year.\"\n  },\n  humanReview: {\n    label: \"Route to Human Review\",\n    hint: \"Send it to a person to look at closely.\"\n  },\n  updateStatement: {\n    label: \"Update the Transparency Statement\",\n    hint: \"Revise what you have told users about the system.\"\n  }\n};\n\nconst ACTION_ORDER = [\"monitor\", \"retrain\", \"humanReview\", \"updateStatement\"];\n\nconst EVENTS = {\n  drift: {\n    label: \"Drift\",\n    staleFields: [\"knownLimits\"],\n    consequences: {\n      retrain: {\n        delta: 8,\n        outcome: \"You retrain on recent data. Accuracy climbs back into the high 80s within a day. The world changed, so the model had to change with it.\"\n      },\n      monitor: {\n        delta: -5,\n        outcome: \"You wait to see if it is a blip. It is not. A week later, performance has slipped even further and more users have noticed. Waiting cost a week on a problem the signal data already flagged.\"\n      },\n      humanReview: {\n        delta: -3,\n        outcome: \"A reviewer confirms real drift, which the signal data already showed. Nothing changes yet. The model still needs someone with authority to retrain it.\"\n      },\n      updateStatement: {\n        delta: -8,\n        outcome: \"You disclose the dip, but the model itself is unchanged. Users keep getting steadily worse results while the documentation says it is a known issue. Disclosure is not a fix.\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  databug: {\n    label: \"Data Bug\",\n    staleFields: [],\n    consequences: {\n      humanReview: {\n        delta: 8,\n        outcome: \"An engineer traces it to a duplicate-logging bug and patches it. The model was fine the whole time. This was never a model problem.\"\n      },\n      retrain: {\n        delta: -12,\n        outcome: \"You retrain on the affected data. The model now learns from the corrupted numbers, baking the bug into future output. You have spent a retrain making things worse.\"\n      },\n      monitor: {\n        delta: -5,\n        outcome: \"You wait. The bad data keeps compounding into other metrics, and by the time anyone investigates it is tangled up with several other numbers. Pipeline bugs do not self-correct.\"\n      },\n      updateStatement: {\n        delta: -3,\n        outcome: \"You revise a limits field to explain the anomaly, but the statement was never the problem. The corrupted pipeline is still corrupted.\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  usageshift: {\n    label: \"Usage Shift\",\n    staleFields: [\"knownLimits\"],\n    consequences: {\n      updateStatement: {\n        delta: 8,\n        outcome: \"You add the new population to your documented limits. Users and your own team now know what to watch for while enough data builds up to retrain responsibly.\"\n      },\n      retrain: {\n        delta: -10,\n        outcome: \"You retrain immediately on only a few days of new data, nowhere near enough to do it responsibly. You have spent a retrain on a half-informed fix, and the gap still is not documented.\"\n      },\n      monitor: {\n        delta: -5,\n        outcome: \"You wait and say nothing. The new users keep getting output tuned for a different population, with no warning that they are outside the system's tested scope.\"\n      },\n      humanReview: {\n        delta: -2,\n        outcome: \"A reviewer confirms the new population looks different from training data, which the signal data already told you. Nothing is disclosed, and the system keeps serving them undocumented.\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  falsealarm: {\n    label: \"False Alarm\",\n    staleFields: [],\n    consequences: {\n      monitor: {\n        delta: 8,\n        outcome: \"You watch the metric for a few hours. It settles back to normal on its own, exactly as a one-off spike should. No fix was needed because nothing was actually broken.\"\n      },\n      retrain: {\n        delta: -12,\n        outcome: \"You retrain on the spike. The model now treats a one-time fluke as a lasting pattern, and normal-day performance gets slightly worse. You have spent a retrain on noise.\"\n      },\n      humanReview: {\n        delta: -3,\n        outcome: \"A reviewer investigates a spike that was already fading on its own. Not harmful, but review time is limited, and this was not the case that needed it.\"\n      },\n      updateStatement: {\n        delta: -5,\n        outcome: \"You add a limits note about the spike. A day later it is irrelevant, and the documentation now has a stale entry describing a problem that no longer exists.\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst EVENT_ORDER = [\"drift\", \"databug\", \"usageshift\", \"falsealarm\"];\n\nconst FIELD_ORDER = [\"purpose\", \"trainingData\", \"knownLimits\"];\nconst FIELD_LABELS = {\n  purpose: \"Purpose\",\n  trainingData: \"Training Data\",\n  knownLimits: \"Known Limits\"\n};\n\n// Questions that force a rewrite rather than a copy of the Spec Card text.\n// knownLimits has no matching Spec Card fact, so it needs no copy-check.\nconst FIELD_PROMPTS = {\n  purpose: \"What does this system do, and who is it for? Explain it the way you would to a user who has never heard of AI.\",\n  trainingData: \"What data trained this system, and what might that leave out? Explain it in plain language.\",\n  knownLimits: \"This one is not on the Spec Card. Based on the Purpose and Training Data, name one specific situation where this system might get it wrong.\"\n};\n\nconst COPY_CHECK_FIELDS = [\"purpose\", \"trainingData\"];\nconst COPY_CHECK_MESSAGE = \"Put this in your own words instead of copying it from the Spec Card.\";\n\nfunction normalizeForComparison(text) {\n  return text.trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+/g, \" \");\n}\n\n// ---------- DOM references ----------\n\nconst appMain = document.getElementById(\"app-main\");\nconst trustBadge = document.getElementById(\"trust-badge\");\nconst trustBadgeValue = document.getElementById(\"trust-badge-value\");\n\n// ---------- Small DOM helper (no innerHTML, ever) ----------\n\nfunction el(tag, attributes, children) {\n  const node = document.createElement(tag);\n  const attrs = attributes || {};\n  Object.keys(attrs).forEach((key) => {\n    if (key === \"class\") {\n      node.className = attrs[key];\n    } else {\n      node.setAttribute(key, attrs[key]);\n    }\n  });\n  (children || []).forEach((child) => {\n    if (typeof child === \"string\") {\n      node.appendChild(document.createTextNode(child));\n    } else if (child) {\n      node.appendChild(child);\n    }\n  });\n  return node;\n}\n\nfunction clearMain() {\n  while (appMain.firstChild) {\n    appMain.removeChild(appMain.firstChild);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction focusHeading(heading) {\n  heading.setAttribute(\"tabindex\", \"-1\");\n  heading.focus();\n}\n\nfunction updateTrustBadge(show) {\n  if (!show) {\n    trustBadge.hidden = true;\n    return;\n  }\n  trustBadge.hidden = false;\n  trustBadgeValue.textContent = String(state.trustScore);\n}\n\nfunction shuffle(items) {\n  const copy = items.slice();\n  for (let i = copy.length - 1; i > 0; i -= 1) {\n    const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));\n    const temp = copy[i];\n    copy[i] = copy[j];\n    copy[j] = temp;\n  }\n  return copy;\n}\n\n// ---------- Game state ----------\n\nlet state = null;\n\nfunction initGame() {\n  state = {\n    systemId: null,\n    statement: {\n      purpose: { value: \"\", history: [] },\n      trainingData: { value: \"\", history: [] },\n      knownLimits: { value: \"\", history: [] }\n    },\n    trustScore: 70,\n    retrainsUsed: 0,\n    order: shuffle(EVENT_ORDER),\n    roundIndex: 0,\n    log: [],\n    pendingActionKey: null,\n    pendingEventId: null\n  };\n}\n\n// ---------- Shared building blocks ----------\n\nfunction buildSpecCard(system) {\n  const card = el(\"dl\", { class: \"spec-card\" });\n  const rows = [\n    [\"Purpose\", system.purpose],\n    [\"Training Data\", system.trainingData],\n    [\"Launch Accuracy Claim\", system.accuracyClaim]\n  ];\n  rows.forEach((row) => {\n    card.appendChild(el(\"dt\", { class: \"spec-card-term\" }, [row[0]]));\n    card.appendChild(el(\"dd\", { class: \"spec-card-value\" }, [row[1]]));\n  });\n  return card;\n}\n\n// ---------- Screen: Intro ----------\n\nfunction renderIntro() {\n  clearMain();\n  updateTrustBadge(false);\n\n  const heading = el(\"h2\", { class: \"screen-heading\" }, [\n    \"Your AI System Just Launched\"\n  ]);\n  const lead = el(\"p\", { class: \"screen-lead\" }, [\n    \"Can you keep it trustworthy for a whole year?\"\n  ]);\n  const body = el(\"p\", { class: \"screen-body\" }, [\n    \"You are about to spend a year in charge of a live AI system. Real people will use it, real things will happen to it, and every choice you make changes what happens next. Four times this year, something happens to your system. How you respond decides whether people can still trust it by the end.\"\n  ]);\n  const startBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-primary btn-large\", type: \"button\" }, [\n    \"Start the Year\"\n  ]);\n  startBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    renderSystemSelect();\n  });\n\n  appMain.appendChild(heading);\n  appMain.appendChild(lead);\n  appMain.appendChild(body);\n  appMain.appendChild(startBtn);\n  focusHeading(heading);\n}\n\n// ---------- Screen: Choose Your System ----------\n\nfunction renderSystemSelect() {\n  clearMain();\n  updateTrustBadge(false);\n\n  const heading = el(\"h2\", { class: \"screen-heading\" }, [\"Choose Your System\"]);\n  const lead = el(\"p\", { class: \"screen-lead\" }, [\n    \"Pick the AI system you will be responsible for this year.\"\n  ]);\n\n  const form = el(\"form\", { class: \"system-form\" });\n  const grid = el(\"div\", { class: \"card-grid\" });\n\n  SYSTEM_ORDER.forEach((systemId) => {\n    const system = SYSTEMS[systemId];\n    const input = el(\"input\", {\n      type: \"radio\",\n      name: \"system\",\n      value: systemId,\n      class: \"system-radio\",\n      required: \"\"\n    });\n    const body = el(\"span\", { class: \"system-card-body\" }, [\n      el(\"span\", { class: \"system-name\" }, [system.name]),\n      el(\"span\", { class: \"system-desc\" }, [system.tagline])\n    ]);\n    const label = el(\"label\", { class: \"system-card\" });\n    label.appendChild(input);\n    label.appendChild(body);\n    grid.appendChild(label);\n  });\n\n  form.appendChild(grid);\n  const continueBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-primary btn-large\", type: \"submit\" }, [\n    \"Continue\"\n  ]);\n  form.appendChild(continueBtn);\n\n  form.addEventListener(\"submit\", (event) => {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    if (!form.checkValidity()) {\n      form.reportValidity();\n      return;\n    }\n    const selected = form.querySelector('input[name=\"system\"]:checked');\n    state.systemId = selected.value;\n    renderSpecCard();\n  });\n\n  appMain.appendChild(heading);\n  appMain.appendChild(lead);\n  appMain.appendChild(form);\n  focusHeading(heading);\n}\n\n// ---------- Screen: Meet Your System ----------\n\nfunction renderSpecCard() {\n  clearMain();\n  updateTrustBadge(false);\n\n  const system = SYSTEMS[state.systemId];\n  const heading = el(\"h2\", { class: \"screen-heading\" }, [\n    \"Meet Your System: \" + system.name\n  ]);\n  const lead = el(\"p\", { class: \"screen-lead\" }, [\n    \"Here is what you know about it so far.\"\n  ]);\n  const specCard = buildSpecCard(system);\n  const continueBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-primary btn-large\", type: \"button\" }, [\n    \"Continue to Your Transparency Statement\"\n  ]);\n  continueBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    renderDraftStatement();\n  });\n\n  appMain.appendChild(heading);\n  appMain.appendChild(lead);\n  appMain.appendChild(specCard);\n  appMain.appendChild(continueBtn);\n  focusHeading(heading);\n}\n\n// ---------- Screen: Draft Transparency Statement ----------\n\nfunction renderDraftStatement() {\n  clearMain();\n  updateTrustBadge(false);\n\n  const system = SYSTEMS[state.systemId];\n  const heading = el(\"h2\", { class: \"screen-heading\" }, [\n    \"Draft Your Transparency Statement\"\n  ]);\n  const lead = el(\"p\", { class: \"screen-lead\" }, [\n    \"Before your system's first year begins, write down what people should know about it. Do not just restate the Spec Card. Write each answer the way you would explain it to a user, in your own words.\"\n  ]);\n\n  const wrap = el(\"div\", { class: \"two-col\" });\n\n  const refCol = el(\"div\", { class: \"two-col-side\" }, [\n    el(\"h3\", { class: \"subheading\" }, [\"Your System\"]),\n    buildSpecCard(system)\n  ]);\n\n  const formCol = el(\"div\", { class: \"two-col-main\" });\n  const form = el(\"form\", { class: \"statement-form\" });\n  const fieldsWrap = el(\"div\", { class: \"field-stack\" });\n\n  FIELD_ORDER.forEach((key) => {\n    const fieldId = \"field-\" + key;\n    const hintId = fieldId + \"-hint\";\n    const label = el(\"label\", { class: \"field-label\", for: fieldId }, [FIELD_LABELS[key]]);\n    const hint = el(\"p\", { class: \"field-hint\", id: hintId }, [FIELD_PROMPTS[key]]);\n    const textarea = el(\"textarea\", {\n      class: \"field-textarea\",\n      id: fieldId,\n      name: key,\n      required: \"\",\n      rows: \"3\",\n      \"aria-describedby\": hintId\n    });\n    textarea.addEventListener(\"input\", () => {\n      textarea.setCustomValidity(\"\");\n    });\n    fieldsWrap.appendChild(el(\"div\", { class: \"field-group\" }, [label, hint, textarea]));\n  });\n\n  form.appendChild(fieldsWrap);\n  const submitBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-primary btn-large\", type: \"submit\" }, [\n    \"Save Statement and Start the Year\"\n  ]);\n  form.appendChild(submitBtn);\n\n  form.addEventListener(\"submit\", (event) => {\n    event.preventDefault();\n\n    COPY_CHECK_FIELDS.forEach((key) => {\n      const textarea = form.elements[key];\n      const matchesSpecCard = normalizeForComparison(textarea.value) === normalizeForComparison(system[key]);\n      textarea.setCustomValidity(matchesSpecCard ? COPY_CHECK_MESSAGE : \"\");\n    });\n\n    if (!form.checkValidity()) {\n      form.reportValidity();\n      return;\n    }\n\n    FIELD_ORDER.forEach((key) => {\n      const value = form.elements[key].value.trim();\n      state.statement[key].value = value;\n      state.statement[key].history.push({ value: value, momentLabel: \"Initial statement\" });\n    });\n    renderRound();\n  });\n\n  formCol.appendChild(form);\n  wrap.appendChild(refCol);\n  wrap.appendChild(formCol);\n\n  appMain.appendChild(heading);\n  appMain.appendChild(lead);\n  appMain.appendChild(wrap);\n  focusHeading(heading);\n}\n\n// ---------- Screen: Round (Event + Decide) ----------\n\nfunction renderRound() {\n  clearMain();\n  updateTrustBadge(true);\n\n  const roundNumber = state.roundIndex + 1;\n  const eventId = state.order[state.roundIndex];\n  const event = EVENTS[eventId];\n  const system = SYSTEMS[state.systemId];\n  const eventContent = system.events[eventId];\n\n  const eyebrow = el(\"p\", { class: \"screen-eyebrow\" }, [\"Round \" + roundNumber + \" of 4\"]);\n  const heading = el(\"h2\", { class: \"screen-heading\" }, [\"Something Happened\"]);\n\n  const eventCard = el(\"div\", { class: \"card event-card\" }, [\n    el(\"p\", { class: \"event-text\" }, [eventContent.text]),\n    el(\"p\", { class: \"event-signal\" }, [\"Signal data: \" + eventContent.signal])\n  ]);\n\n  const form = el(\"form\", { class: \"decide-form\" });\n  const fieldset = el(\"fieldset\", { class: \"action-fieldset\" });\n  fieldset.appendChild(el(\"legend\", { class: \"action-legend\" }, [\"Choose your action\"]));\n\n  const actionGrid = el(\"div\", { class: \"action-grid\" });\n\n  ACTION_ORDER.forEach((actionKey) => {\n    const action = ACTIONS[actionKey];\n    const isRetrain = actionKey === \"retrain\";\n    const usesLeft = 2 - state.retrainsUsed;\n    const disabled = isRetrain && usesLeft <= 0;\n\n    const input = el(\"input\", {\n      type: \"radio\",\n      name: \"action\",\n      value: actionKey,\n      class: \"action-radio\",\n      required: \"\"\n    });\n    if (disabled) {\n      input.setAttribute(\"disabled\", \"\");\n    }\n\n    const bodyChildren = [\n      el(\"span\", { class: \"action-name\" }, [action.label]),\n      el(\"span\", { class: \"action-hint\" }, [action.hint])\n    ];\n\n    if (isRetrain) {\n      const remainingText = usesLeft <= 0\n        ? \"No uses left this year\"\n        : usesLeft + (usesLeft === 1 ? \" use left this year\" : \" uses left this year\");\n      bodyChildren.push(el(\"span\", { class: \"action-remaining\" }, [remainingText]));\n    }\n\n    const body = el(\"span\", { class: \"action-card-body\" }, bodyChildren);\n    const label = el(\"label\", { class: \"action-card\" });\n    if (disabled) {\n      label.classList.add(\"action-card-disabled\");\n    }\n    label.appendChild(input);\n    label.appendChild(body);\n    actionGrid.appendChild(label);\n  });\n\n  fieldset.appendChild(actionGrid);\n  form.appendChild(fieldset);\n\n  const justifyGroup = el(\"div\", { class: \"field-group\" });\n  const justifyLabel = el(\"label\", { class: \"field-label\", for: \"justification\" }, [\n    \"Explain your decision in one sentence.\"\n  ]);\n  const justifyArea = el(\"textarea\", {\n    class: \"field-textarea\",\n    id: \"justification\",\n    name: \"justification\",\n    required: \"\",\n    rows: \"2\"\n  });\n  justifyGroup.appendChild(justifyLabel);\n  justifyGroup.appendChild(justifyArea);\n  form.appendChild(justifyGroup);\n\n  const submitBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-primary btn-large\", type: \"submit\" }, [\n    \"Submit Your Decision\"\n  ]);\n  form.appendChild(submitBtn);\n\n  form.addEventListener(\"submit\", (submitEvent) => {\n    submitEvent.preventDefault();\n    if (!form.checkValidity()) {\n      form.reportValidity();\n      return;\n    }\n    const chosen = form.querySelector('input[name=\"action\"]:checked');\n    if (!chosen) {\n      form.reportValidity();\n      return;\n    }\n    handleDecision(eventId, chosen.value, justifyArea.value.trim());\n  });\n\n  appMain.appendChild(eyebrow);\n  appMain.appendChild(heading);\n  appMain.appendChild(eventCard);\n  appMain.appendChild(form);\n  focusHeading(heading);\n}\n\nfunction handleDecision(eventId, actionKey, justification) {\n  const event = EVENTS[eventId];\n  const consequence = event.consequences[actionKey];\n\n  state.trustScore += consequence.delta;\n  if (actionKey === \"retrain\") {\n    state.retrainsUsed += 1;\n  }\n\n  const logEntry = {\n    roundNumber: state.roundIndex + 1,\n    eventId: eventId,\n    eventLabel: event.label,\n    actionLabel: ACTIONS[actionKey].label,\n    justification: justification,\n    outcome: consequence.outcome,\n    delta: consequence.delta,\n    resultingScore: state.trustScore\n  };\n  state.log.push(logEntry);\n  state.pendingActionKey = actionKey;\n  state.pendingEventId = eventId;\n\n  renderResults(logEntry);\n}\n\n// ---------- Screen: Results ----------\n\nfunction renderResults(logEntry) {\n  clearMain();\n  updateTrustBadge(true);\n\n  const heading = el(\"h2\", { class: \"screen-heading\" }, [\"Here Is What Happened\"]);\n  const outcome = el(\"p\", { class: \"card results-outcome\" }, [logEntry.outcome]);\n\n  const deltaText = logEntry.delta >= 0\n    ? \"up \" + logEntry.delta + \" points\"\n    : \"down \" + Math.abs(logEntry.delta) + \" points\";\n  const scoreLine = el(\"p\", { class: \"results-score-line\" }, [\n    \"Trust Score: \" + logEntry.resultingScore + \" out of 100 (\" + deltaText + \").\"\n  ]);\n\n  const detailsWrap = el(\"div\", { class: \"counterfactual-list\" });\n  detailsWrap.appendChild(el(\"h3\", { class: \"subheading\" }, [\"What if you had chosen differently?\"]));\n\n  const otherActions = ACTION_ORDER.filter((key) => key !== state.pendingActionKey);\n  otherActions.forEach((key) => {\n    const consequence = EVENTS[state.pendingEventId].consequences[key];\n    const details = el(\"details\", { class: \"counterfactual-details\" });\n    const summary = el(\"summary\", { class: \"counterfactual-summary\" }, [\n      \"What if you had chosen: \" + ACTIONS[key].label + \"?\"\n    ]);\n    const text = el(\"p\", { class: \"counterfactual-text\" }, [consequence.outcome]);\n    details.appendChild(summary);\n    details.appendChild(text);\n    detailsWrap.appendChild(details);\n  });\n\n  const continueBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-primary btn-large\", type: \"button\" }, [\n    \"Continue\"\n  ]);\n  continueBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    afterResults();\n  });\n\n  appMain.appendChild(heading);\n  appMain.appendChild(outcome);\n  appMain.appendChild(scoreLine);\n  appMain.appendChild(detailsWrap);\n  appMain.appendChild(continueBtn);\n  focusHeading(heading);\n}\n\nfunction afterResults() {\n  const event = EVENTS[state.pendingEventId];\n  if (event.staleFields.length > 0) {\n    renderMaintain(event.staleFields);\n  } else {\n    advanceRound();\n  }\n}\n\nfunction advanceRound() {\n  state.roundIndex += 1;\n  if (state.roundIndex >= state.order.length) {\n    renderYearInReview();\n  } else {\n    renderRound();\n  }\n}\n\n// ---------- Screen: Maintain Statement ----------\n\nfunction renderMaintain(staleFields) {\n  clearMain();\n  updateTrustBadge(true);\n\n  const heading = el(\"h2\", { class: \"screen-heading\" }, [\"Update Your Transparency Statement\"]);\n  const lead = el(\"p\", { class: \"screen-lead\" }, [\n    \"What just happened changed how your system actually behaves. Update the field below so your statement still tells the truth, or skip and take a trust penalty.\"\n  ]);\n\n  const form = el(\"form\", { class: \"maintain-form\" });\n  const fieldsWrap = el(\"div\", { class: \"field-stack\" });\n\n  staleFields.forEach((key) => {\n    const fieldId = \"maintain-\" + key;\n    const flag = el(\"p\", { class: \"stale-flag\" }, [FIELD_LABELS[key] + \": out of date\"]);\n    const label = el(\"label\", { class: \"field-label\", for: fieldId }, [\"Revise: \" + FIELD_LABELS[key]]);\n    const textarea = el(\"textarea\", {\n      class: \"field-textarea\",\n      id: fieldId,\n      name: key,\n      rows: \"3\"\n    });\n    textarea.value = state.statement[key].value;\n    fieldsWrap.appendChild(el(\"div\", { class: \"field-group\" }, [flag, label, textarea]));\n  });\n\n  form.appendChild(fieldsWrap);\n\n  const buttonRow = el(\"div\", { class: \"button-row\" });\n  const saveBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-primary btn-large\", type: \"submit\" }, [\"Save Update\"]);\n  const skipBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-secondary btn-large\", type: \"button\" }, [\n    \"Skip (Trust Score minus 5)\"\n  ]);\n  buttonRow.appendChild(saveBtn);\n  buttonRow.appendChild(skipBtn);\n  form.appendChild(buttonRow);\n\n  form.addEventListener(\"submit\", (event) => {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    const eventLabel = EVENTS[state.pendingEventId].label;\n    staleFields.forEach((key) => {\n      const value = form.elements[key].value.trim();\n      state.statement[key].value = value;\n      state.statement[key].history.push({\n        value: value,\n        momentLabel: \"After Round \" + (state.roundIndex + 1) + \" (\" + eventLabel + \")\"\n      });\n    });\n    advanceRound();\n  });\n\n  skipBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    state.trustScore -= 5;\n    advanceRound();\n  });\n\n  appMain.appendChild(heading);\n  appMain.appendChild(lead);\n  appMain.appendChild(form);\n  focusHeading(heading);\n}\n\n// ---------- Screen: Year in Review ----------\n\nfunction renderYearInReview() {\n  clearMain();\n  updateTrustBadge(true);\n\n  const heading = el(\"h2\", { class: \"screen-heading\" }, [\"Year in Review\"]);\n  const scoreLine = el(\"p\", { class: \"screen-lead\" }, [\n    \"Your system finishes the year with a Trust Score of \" + state.trustScore + \" out of 100.\"\n  ]);\n\n  const logHeading = el(\"h3\", { class: \"subheading\" }, [\"Your Decision Log\"]);\n  const table = buildLogTable();\n\n  const statementHeading = el(\"h3\", { class: \"subheading\" }, [\"Your Transparency Statement\"]);\n  const statementBlock = buildStatementReview();\n\n  const turnInHeading = el(\"h3\", { class: \"subheading\" }, [\"Turn This In\"]);\n  const turnInLead = el(\"p\", { class: \"screen-body\" }, [\n    \"If your teacher wants you to turn this in, you can screenshot this page, or copy the text below into your Activity Guide.\"\n  ]);\n  const turnInBlock = buildTurnInBlock();\n\n  const restartBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-secondary btn-large\", type: \"button\" }, [\n    \"Start a New Year\"\n  ]);\n  restartBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    initGame();\n    renderIntro();\n  });\n\n  appMain.appendChild(heading);\n  appMain.appendChild(scoreLine);\n  appMain.appendChild(logHeading);\n  appMain.appendChild(table);\n  appMain.appendChild(statementHeading);\n  appMain.appendChild(statementBlock);\n  appMain.appendChild(turnInHeading);\n  appMain.appendChild(turnInLead);\n  appMain.appendChild(turnInBlock);\n  appMain.appendChild(restartBtn);\n  focusHeading(heading);\n}\n\nfunction buildSummaryText() {\n  const lines = [];\n  lines.push(\"Trust Score: \" + state.trustScore + \" out of 100\");\n  lines.push(\"\");\n  lines.push(\"DECISION LOG\");\n\n  state.log.forEach((entry) => {\n    const deltaText = entry.delta >= 0 ? \"+\" + entry.delta : String(entry.delta);\n    lines.push(\"\");\n    lines.push(\"Round \" + entry.roundNumber + \" - \" + entry.eventLabel);\n    lines.push(\"Your action: \" + entry.actionLabel);\n    lines.push(\"Your justification: \" + entry.justification);\n    lines.push(\"What happened: \" + entry.outcome);\n    lines.push(\"Trust change: \" + deltaText);\n  });\n\n  lines.push(\"\");\n  lines.push(\"TRANSPARENCY STATEMENT\");\n  FIELD_ORDER.forEach((key) => {\n    lines.push(\"\");\n    lines.push(FIELD_LABELS[key] + \": \" + (state.statement[key].value || \"Not written.\"));\n  });\n\n  return lines.join(\"\\n\");\n}\n\nfunction buildTurnInBlock() {\n  const wrap = el(\"div\", { class: \"turn-in-block\" });\n  const labelId = \"summary-text-label\";\n  const hintId = \"summary-text-hint\";\n\n  const label = el(\"label\", { class: \"field-label\", for: \"summary-text\", id: labelId }, [\n    \"Your summary (read-only)\"\n  ]);\n  const hint = el(\"p\", { class: \"field-hint\", id: hintId }, [\n    \"Click inside the box below to highlight everything, then press Ctrl+C (or Cmd+C on Mac) to copy it.\"\n  ]);\n\n  const textarea = el(\"textarea\", {\n    class: \"field-textarea summary-textarea\",\n    id: \"summary-text\",\n    readonly: \"\",\n    rows: \"10\",\n    \"aria-describedby\": hintId\n  });\n  textarea.value = buildSummaryText();\n  textarea.addEventListener(\"focus\", () => {\n    textarea.select();\n  });\n\n  const selectAllBtn = el(\"button\", { class: \"btn btn-secondary\", type: \"button\" }, [\n    \"Select All Text\"\n  ]);\n  selectAllBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    textarea.focus();\n    textarea.select();\n  });\n\n  wrap.appendChild(label);\n  wrap.appendChild(hint);\n  wrap.appendChild(textarea);\n  wrap.appendChild(selectAllBtn);\n  return wrap;\n}\n\nfunction buildLogTable() {\n  const wrap = el(\"div\", { class: \"table-scroll\" });\n  const table = el(\"table\", { class: \"log-table\" });\n  const caption = el(\"caption\", {}, [\"Every round, in order, with the action you chose and what happened.\"]);\n\n  const thead = el(\"thead\");\n  const headRow = el(\"tr\");\n  [\"Round\", \"Event\", \"Your Action\", \"Your Justification\", \"What Happened\", \"Trust Change\"].forEach((label) => {\n    headRow.appendChild(el(\"th\", { scope: \"col\" }, [label]));\n  });\n  thead.appendChild(headRow);\n\n  const tbody = el(\"tbody\");\n  state.log.forEach((entry) => {\n    const row = el(\"tr\");\n    row.appendChild(el(\"th\", { scope: \"row\" }, [String(entry.roundNumber)]));\n    row.appendChild(el(\"td\", {}, [entry.eventLabel]));\n    row.appendChild(el(\"td\", {}, [entry.actionLabel]));\n    row.appendChild(el(\"td\", {}, [entry.justification]));\n    row.appendChild(el(\"td\", {}, [entry.outcome]));\n    const deltaText = entry.delta >= 0 ? \"+\" + entry.delta : String(entry.delta);\n    row.appendChild(el(\"td\", {}, [deltaText]));\n    tbody.appendChild(row);\n  });\n\n  table.appendChild(caption);\n  table.appendChild(thead);\n  table.appendChild(tbody);\n  wrap.appendChild(table);\n  return wrap;\n}\n\nfunction buildStatementReview() {\n  const wrap = el(\"div\", { class: \"statement-review\" });\n\n  FIELD_ORDER.forEach((key) => {\n    const field = state.statement[key];\n    const block = el(\"div\", { class: \"statement-field\" });\n    block.appendChild(el(\"h4\", { class: \"statement-field-label\" }, [FIELD_LABELS[key]]));\n    block.appendChild(el(\"p\", { class: \"statement-field-value\" }, [field.value || \"Not written.\"]));\n\n    if (field.history.length > 1) {\n      const details = el(\"details\", { class: \"version-history\" });\n      details.appendChild(el(\"summary\", {}, [\"Version history\"]));\n      const list = el(\"ol\", { class: \"version-history-list\" });\n      field.history.forEach((version) => {\n        list.appendChild(el(\"li\", {}, [version.momentLabel + \": \" + version.value]));\n      });\n      details.appendChild(list);\n      block.appendChild(details);\n    }\n\n    wrap.appendChild(block);\n  });\n\n  return wrap;\n}\n\n// ---------- Startup ----------\n\nfunction showFatalError() {\n  clearMain();\n  const message = el(\"p\", { class: \"fatal-error\" }, [\n    \"Something went wrong loading this activity. Try reloading the page.\"\n  ]);\n  appMain.appendChild(message);\n}\n\ndocument.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n  try {\n    initGame();\n    renderIntro();\n  } catch (error) {\n    showFatalError();\n  }\n});",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "1",
        "2",
        "3"
      ]
    },
    "long_instructions": "#Keep It Running\r\n\r\nYou and your partner just launched an AI system. You are in charge of keeping it trustworthy for its first year.\r\n\r\n1. Choose the system you and your partner run this year.\r\n2. Read your system's Spec Card, then write your own transparency statement in your own words. You need this written before the year can start.\r\n3. Play through four rounds. Each round, something happens to your system. Choose an action, explain your reasoning in one sentence, and see what happens.\r\n4. If a screen tells you your statement is out of date, update it before you continue. There is no single right action for every event — think about what actually happened before you decide.\r\n5. At the end of the year, review your Trust Score, your Decision Log, and your transparency statement together.\r\n\r\n\r\n"
  },
